  "description": "White field charged at the centre with a red heraldic rose with green leaves.",
  "history": "The first flag of Reus was made in silk in 1774 and was in use until 1943; it was crimson red with the arms at the centre. As the historic arms were a heraldic rose on a silver field, the new flag was white with a heraldic rose at the centre; since 1943 various minor variations of the rose have been used without changing the general appearance of the flag.",
